Subject: [PATCH] Judge session_range_breakout as a portfolio, not one leg at a
 time

SRB_UNCORRELATED_SWEEP passed 0 of 262 cells and named the test it had not run: several
near-zero-correlated legs summed into ONE series before judging. This builds that series under
membership rules fixed in the module and feeds it to the SEALED gauntlet unmodified.

MEASURED on this box, 16 baskets from 262 legs rebuilt out of the gauntlet's own cache (Sharpe
reproduction error 5e-5): ZERO pass. Diversification is real -- the best out-of-sample basket
lifts its members' mean Sharpe 0.0842 to 0.2964, a 3.5x multiple on 21.5 effective independent
bets out of 32 members -- and still reaches only 0.949x of the sealed hurdle 0.3122, dsr 0.332
against 0.95, with deflated_sharpe its ONLY failed gate.

Two findings that matter more than the shortfall:

  * THE UNSELECTED BASKETS LOSE. all_judged -0.8015, block_longest_history -0.5844,
    block_most_liquid -0.9621. Traded the way the rule would actually be deployed this mechanism
    is negative; the positive baskets exist only after a membership filter.
  * THE IN-SAMPLE BASKETS ARE NOT EVIDENCE. A sign-flip null runs the identical select-then-sum
    procedure on legs with NO edge and scores HIGHER than the real data: +1.06 mean (p95 +1.30)
    against the real +0.2665, and +1.23 (p95 +1.46) against the real top-8 +0.3197. p=1.0 both.

Costs are per leg by construction, each member's own Costs and its own 3x arm summed after
charging. gate_spec.yaml was not touched, no threshold moved, nothing added to any live book:
run_gauntlet is called directly so no gate ledger, certificate or authority file is written.

Hourly leg `srb_basket_judge` (portfolio layer); artifact reports/SRB_BASKET_JUDGEMENT.json.

